# AquaPulse Project Baseline

- Keep changes focused and minimal; prefer reusing existing app patterns before introducing new abstractions.
- Do not add broad file-level ignores (for example `ignore_for_file`) unless there is a documented, temporary reason.
- Keep side effects out of build methods; run navigation, dialogs, and state writes from explicit handlers/listeners.
- After an async gap, check `mounted` before `setState`, `Navigator`, or UI feedback calls.
- Keep domain logic in providers/services and keep screens/widgets focused on presentation and user orchestration.
- Reuse centralized style tokens (`NeumorphicStyle` and app theme) instead of ad-hoc colors, radii, and text styles.

## Quick Checks Before Finishing

- Errors are surfaced to users with a consistent UI pattern (not debug-only logs).
- New UI code uses existing shared widgets/utilities when they already fit.
- Dead or "old reference" code is removed instead of being kept in production paths.
